     "id": "yui_3_17_2_1_1788905620687_469",
     "type": "text",
     "html": "<h1>Tui Hills Wedding Photographer</h1><p>Tucked into the edge of the Waitakere Ranges, Tui Hills is one of the most distinctly New Zealand settings I've had the chance to photograph a wedding in — native bush, ferns, and nikau palms standing in for the manicured gardens you'll find at most Auckland venues. It's thirty minutes from town, but it feels like a different world entirely.</p><h2>A setting that does the work for you</h2><p>Every corner of the grounds offers something different to shoot against — dense native bush for portraits with real depth and texture, open lawn for the ceremony itself, and pockets of native garden that catch soft, filtered light through the afternoon. For a couple wanting their photographs to feel unmistakably of this country rather than generic, Tui Hills is hard to beat.</p><p>‍  ‍</p><h2>Why I love photographing here</h2><p>‍I photographed Ellie &amp; Ryan's wedding at Tui Hills, and it's stayed with me since — the venue has a way of making a big day feel grounded and unhurried, exactly the kind of atmosphere that produces the candid, quiet moments alongside the romantic portraits I look for at every wedding. You can read about their day here: <a href=\"https://www.momentsinlight.co.nz/blog/ellie-and-ryan-tui-hills\">Ellie &amp; Ryan's wedding at Tui Hills</a>.</p><p>‍  ‍</p><h2>Thinking about Tui Hills for your wedding?</h2><p>If you're picturing a native bush backdrop and a setting with real New Zealand character, I'd love to talk through what your day at Tui Hills could look like. <a href=\"https://www.momentsinlight.co.nz/contact\">Get in touch</a> to check availability and start planning your photography.</p>",
